{% lede %}
For Optical Electronics, Prof. Gary Eden's course on how lasers work at the University of Illinois, I redrew diagrams and plots from the literature so the ideas were easier to see.
{% /lede %}

The originals came from textbooks and papers, each in its own style: grey shading, black boxes, crowded labels. I redrew them as one set, in a consistent style: color-coded components, a clear beam path, and labels next to what they name.

Seen side by side, the redraws show what consistent visual language adds: the same information, faster to read.
